# Uniform Nested Typing

See [README DragController](../../README.md#dragcontroller) and [mouse-interaction.mdc](mouse-interaction.mdc).

## Uniform EMapped / typed lists

When a card's `nested` is a homogeneous `EMapped` (or other typed collection) of one card kind, trust the generated element type from `childCardAtCoord` / `nested.forEach`. Do **not** guard with `typeName === "…"`.

Keep `typeName` filters only for **heterogeneous** collections (e.g. `seg.cards` mixing header kinds in the periodic table).

To keep nests homogeneous when a parent would otherwise mix card kinds, use the [Type Partition Pattern](../../README.md#type-partition-pattern): intermediate list cards (one per kind) that omit `selfPos` and stretch to the parent.

Incorrect:

```typescript
const hit = listCard.childCardAtCoord(local);
if (!hit || hit.typeName !== "LessonCard") {
  return;
}
drag.begin(hit, event);

siblingList.nested.forEach((nested) => {
  if (nested.typeName === "LessonCard" && nested.attrs.id === lessonId) {
    nested.fire();
  }
});
```

Correct:

```typescript
const hit = listCard.childCardAtCoord(local);
if (!hit) {
  return;
}
drag.begin(hit, event);

siblingList.nested.forEach((nested) => {
  if (nested.attrs.id === lessonId) {
    nested.fire();
  }
});
```

## No redundant region identity checks

When a shared `callbackTable` entry fans events to several region-scoped `DragController`s, do **not** compare `listCard` / `self` to the bound region card inside each handler. `DragController.begin` already no-ops via `containsCard` when the hit card is not nested under that controller's `regionCard`; `move` / `end` no-op when no session was started.

Incorrect:

```typescript
handleMouseDown(listCard, event) {
  if (listCard !== this.lessonListCard) {
    return;
  }
  // …
}
```

Correct — use the event's `self` for coord hit-testing; let `containsCard` scope the region:

```typescript
handleMouseDown(listCard, event) {
  const hit = listCard.childCardAtCoord(event.local);
  if (!hit) {
    return;
  }
  this.dragController.begin(hit, event);
}
```

## Single-use helpers

Prefer inlining a private method used at one call site (e.g. put reschedule logic directly in `updateAttrs` instead of `tryReschedule`).
